  {
    "sha": "5ad46c819f49998a8aede9ae56297b88aabf3a5a",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDVhZDQ2YzgxOWY0OTk5OGE4YWVkZTlhZTU2Mjk3Yjg4YWFiZjNhNWE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T02:47:33Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T02:47:33Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(drilling): Drill, Bore and Thread take a start and an exit pick as the hole order\n\nDrill, Bore and Thread (mill) cut their holes in the list order and\nrefused a start or exit pick as \"not taken\". The three kinds now answer\nPickCapability::HoleOrder: the hole under the start pick is cut first,\nthe hole under the exit pick is cut last, and the holes between keep the\nlist order, rotated to the start hole (camcraft_motion::drilling::\nhole_order). With no pick the hole list is unchanged, so every earlier\nprogram is byte-identical.\n\nRefused by name, never moved: a pick that is on no hole, a start and an\nexit pick on one hole of a longer list, a pick on a Drill with cross\nholes, and a pick on a lathe's axial Drill. The door (named_refusal)\nrefuses the first three; the generator checks again and owns the lathe\nrefusal.\n\nThe operation page draws typed First hole / Last hole rows for the three\nkinds. MCP edit_operation sets the picks through EditOperationParams.\n\nFixes #3328\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
